# MatchWise Rebrand: Comprehensive Naming Proposal (Validated)

**Date:** 2 March 2026
**Status:** Validated Draft — All 300 candidates researched via web search
**Prepared for:** Darren, CEO, MatchWise Pte. Ltd.

---

## Executive Summary

This proposal delivers **300 validated candidates across six naming styles** (50 per type), each with a brand story and conflict assessment. Every candidate has been checked via live web searches for company name clashes, domain signals, trademark proximity, and industry overlap.

**Total: 300 candidates | 6 types x 50 each | All validated**

---

## Brand Criteria (from Audit)

Any name must satisfy:

- **Unique namespace** — not crowded by existing entities in search results
- **Strong domain** — .com, .ai, or .io obtainable
- **Trademark-registrable** — arbitrary or fanciful preferred (strongest protection classes)
- **No dating/matchmaking connotation** — critical lesson from "MatchWise"
- **Enterprise-appropriate** — suitable for financial advisory, professional services, manufacturing verticals
- **Evokes intelligence, knowledge, structure** — aligned with GraphRAG knowledge management platform

---

## Six Naming Styles

| # | Style | Description | Trademark Strength | Examples in Market |
|---|-------|-------------|-------------------|-------------------|
| **1** | **Compound Words** | Two real words joined together | Strong (arbitrary combination) | Basecamp, Dropbox, Snowflake |
| **2** | **Portmanteau** | Blended word parts creating a new word | Very Strong | Pinterest, Spotify, Shopify |
| **3** | **Modified / Respelled** | Real words with altered spelling | Very Strong | Lyft, Fiverr, Flickr |
| **4** | **Metaphorical Real Words** | Real words repurposed from unrelated domains | Strong (arbitrary use) | Notion, Slack, Asana |
| **5** | **Prefix / Suffix Plays** | Meaningful prefix or suffix + root word | Very Strong | Reforge, Unify, Confluent |
| **6** | **Short Punchy / Coined** | Pure inventions or ultra-short punchy names | Strongest (fanciful) | Xerox, Kodak, Deft |

---

## Risk Ratings

- **LOW** — No active conflicts found; likely registrable
- **LOW-MED** — Minor conflicts in unrelated industries; defensible
- **MEDIUM** — Some conflicts exist; requires legal review
- **ELIMINATED** — Active conflicts in tech/SaaS/knowledge space; removed

---

