| 16 | **Filaro** | "Filo" (Italian: thread) + warm "-aro". Threading together. | LOW | The elegance of a single thread connecting everything — documents, people, insights. "We thread your knowledge together." Short, warm, visually clean. The "-aro" ending matches Canva/Asana energy. | No match found. "Filigran" (cybersecurity) and "Filora" (agriculture) are different. Clean. |
| 17 | **Pensaro** | "Pensare" (Italian: to think). Deep thought, wisdom. | LOW-MED | Thoughtful, structured thinking — seeing how everything connects. "We help you think better." Italian root gives artisan quality without being pretentious. | Pensero AI (engineering management, 2024) exists with similar root. Different name/spelling. |
| 18 | **Cureva** | "Curate" + warm "-eva". Curation, care. | LOW-MED | The art of curation — carefully selecting and presenting knowledge. "Your knowledge, expertly curated." Gentle sound avoids tech coldness while conveying competence. | Cureva Health (medical tourism, India) and Cureva Lifesciences (pharma). Medical connotation risk. |
| 19 | **Talena** | "Tale" + warm "-ena". Story, narrative. | LOW-MED | Knowledge is not just data — it is stories and expertise. "We help you tell the story of what you know." Simple, warm, memorable. | Talena Inc. (San Jose, ML data management) and Talena Vita (Ukraine workforce). Existing uses create risk. |
| 20 | **Kavelo** | "Cave" (explore) + warm "-elo". Exploration, depth. | LOW-MED | An invitation to explore — venture into your organization's knowledge and come back with what you need. Same warm energy as Canva or Asana. "Explore with confidence." | Cavelo (cybersecurity DSPM) is close in spelling and in tech. LOW-MED due to proximity. |

